WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:04.940
Today, I'd like to introduce you all 
to your new classmate.

00:04.940 --> 00:07.920
<b><i>Kurose
Maria</i></b>

00:05.410 --> 00:07.180
My name is Kurose Maria.

00:07.900 --> 00:09.360
Whoa!

00:09.740 --> 00:11.930
Oh damn! She's way too cute!

00:11.930 --> 00:13.860
She looks so prim and proper!

00:12.690 --> 00:14.820
She's super pretty!

00:17.120 --> 00:18.470
Kurose-san...

00:23.570 --> 00:24.920
Sorry, I can't.

00:25.760 --> 00:30.220
Kashima-kun, I still think of you 
as a good friend.

00:33.580 --> 00:35.220
<i>I-It's okay.</i>

00:35.720 --> 00:40.260
<i>Because right now I have Shirakawa-san, 
and she's a wonderful girlfriend!</i>

00:40.640 --> 00:42.890
Kurose-san, please introduce yourself.

00:40.640 --> 00:44.350
<b><i>Kurose Maria</i></b>

00:42.890 --> 00:43.860
Okay.

00:44.350 --> 00:47.870
I moved back to the area 
after three years away.

00:47.870 --> 00:52.820
I don't know a lot about this school yet, 
so I hope you all can teach me.

00:52.820 --> 00:54.280
Sure!

00:54.650 --> 00:56.510
Thank you very much!

00:56.510 --> 00:58.180
It's nice to meet you all.

01:01.130 --> 01:05.800
<i>She probably has no reason to remember 
that part of her history with me.</i>

01:06.200 --> 01:09.290
<i>I should just try to stay away from her.</i>

01:10.100 --> 01:14.940
I guess Kurose-san should sit somewhere 
she can ask questions easily,

01:14.940 --> 01:16.490
so how about here?

01:16.490 --> 01:17.300
Huh?

01:18.770 --> 01:19.540
What?

01:22.010 --> 01:24.980
What?!

01:36.450 --> 01:43.080
<b>Our Dating Story: 
The Experienced You and The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:55.020 --> 03:01.780
<b>My Surprise For You Story:</b>

02:55.550 --> 03:01.780
<b>The Experienced You and</b>

02:56.050 --> 03:01.780
<b>The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:56.070 --> 02:57.230
For real?

02:57.230 --> 02:59.070
That's crazy.

03:00.480 --> 03:01.780
Um...

03:02.120 --> 03:04.060
You're Kashima-kun, right?

03:04.790 --> 03:05.990
Mm-hmm.

03:05.990 --> 03:08.260
I knew it was you, Kashima-kun!

03:08.700 --> 03:12.480
We get to be neighbors again. 
What a coincidence!

03:12.480 --> 03:13.710
Let's be friends, okay?

03:13.710 --> 03:16.420
Yeah. L-Let's be friends.

03:17.280 --> 03:18.250
Huh?

03:18.250 --> 03:21.130
Oh. We went to the same middle school.

03:21.130 --> 03:24.430
Yeah, but I'm still Team Shirakawa-san.

03:24.430 --> 03:26.720
I'm going for Kurose-san now.

03:26.720 --> 03:32.160
<i>With people talking, it could come up. 
People might find out I asked her out.</i>

03:32.160 --> 03:37.340
<i>Yeah. I've got to stay far away 
from Kurose-san!</i>

03:45.040 --> 03:47.030
Your hair is so pretty!

03:47.030 --> 03:49.100
Oh, not really.

03:49.100 --> 03:50.960
I wish mine was that shiny.

03:50.960 --> 03:52.540
Don't be silly.

03:58.480 --> 04:00.510
You. Kashima Ryuto.

04:02.340 --> 04:04.500
<i>She appeared! The hardcore gyaru!</i>

04:05.200 --> 04:07.680
Y-Yes? May I help you?

04:07.680 --> 04:09.610
I need you for something.

04:19.880 --> 04:23.930
Um, excuse me, Yamana-san.

04:24.730 --> 04:27.910
Have I... done something wrong?

04:27.910 --> 04:28.860
Huh?

04:28.860 --> 04:30.800
Wh-What do you want me for?

04:30.800 --> 04:32.120
Fries, you know,

04:32.460 --> 04:34.670
they taste like shit when they get cold.

04:34.670 --> 04:36.620
Will you let me finish eating first?

04:37.580 --> 04:39.140
S-Sure.

04:53.410 --> 04:54.800
I mean, like,

04:54.800 --> 04:58.610
next Sunday is Runa's birthday. 
Did you know that?

05:00.070 --> 05:02.940
Seriously? You actually didn't know.

05:02.940 --> 05:04.530
R-Right.

05:04.530 --> 05:05.490
Dude!

05:06.050 --> 05:07.470
Are you even serious about Runa?

05:07.470 --> 05:09.870
I-I am serious!

05:09.870 --> 05:13.580
If you're dating, isn't her birthday 
the first thing you should ask about?

05:13.580 --> 05:14.910
I-I'm very sorry!

05:15.960 --> 05:17.120
Fine. Whatever.

05:17.120 --> 05:18.940
So, get this.

05:18.940 --> 05:22.560
Runa's birthday. You're gonna celebrate it.

05:22.560 --> 05:24.160
Uh, yes!

05:24.160 --> 05:29.640
Anyway, I just wanted to tell you that 
when Runa wasn't around.

05:31.840 --> 05:32.860
U-Um...?

05:32.860 --> 05:33.720
What now?

05:33.720 --> 05:37.710
Can you tell me what kinds of things 
Shirakawa-san likes?

05:37.710 --> 05:39.690
I want to give her a birthday present.

05:39.690 --> 05:42.640
What the hell is that? 
Can't you ask her yourself?

05:42.640 --> 05:44.520
Wouldn't it be quicker?

05:44.520 --> 05:49.210
See this Osausa phone case? 
Shirakawa-san gave it to me.

05:49.210 --> 05:50.410
Yeah, I know.

05:51.060 --> 05:55.500
She surprised me with it 
as a one-week anniversary present.

05:55.500 --> 05:58.960
This time, I want to 
surprise her with something.

06:01.110 --> 06:02.670
Got it.

06:03.600 --> 06:06.780
But you'd better make her really happy.

06:06.780 --> 06:08.620
Th-Thank you very much!

06:18.760 --> 06:20.340
Good morning, Ryuto!

06:20.340 --> 06:21.230
Huh?

06:21.230 --> 06:23.740
Good morning. Wait... why?

06:24.660 --> 06:28.150
Well, you know I can't talk to you at school.

06:28.150 --> 06:30.490
Y-Yeah, but still...

06:30.490 --> 06:31.680
This for real?

06:31.680 --> 06:32.120
Huh?

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
<i>Yuna,   Akari</i>

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
Yesterday

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
Yuna

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
Nicole went on a date
 with that dork from class

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
Akari

06:32.120 --> 06:33.330
Really? OMG that's hilarious

06:33.330 --> 06:35.850
Yuna

06:33.330 --> 06:35.850
Nicole went on a date with that dork from class

06:33.330 --> 06:36.250
<i>Nicole went on a date 
with that dork from class.</i>

06:35.910 --> 06:38.600
Really? OMG that's hilarious

06:35.990 --> 06:38.600
Akari

06:36.250 --> 06:38.760
<i>Really? Oh my god, that's hilarious.</i>

06:45.160 --> 06:47.380
Did you hang out with Nicole?

06:47.380 --> 06:51.540
Uh, well, yeah. Um...

06:52.090 --> 06:55.600
Shirakawa-san, are you free next Sunday?

06:55.600 --> 06:58.000
Huh? Sunday?

06:58.000 --> 06:59.440
Yeah, I'm free.

06:59.440 --> 07:03.150
Will you let me celebrate 
your birthday with you, then?

07:03.760 --> 07:07.450
Yamana-san told me. That it's your birthday.

07:07.860 --> 07:10.240
Oh, what? So that's why?

07:10.240 --> 07:11.960
Yeah. Sorry.

07:11.960 --> 07:16.200
Since the topic was going to come up,
I figured I should ask you out first.

07:17.350 --> 07:19.160
I guess it's okay.

07:19.480 --> 07:21.370
I spaced out.

07:21.830 --> 07:25.840
I forgot to ask when your birthday was. Sorry.

07:25.840 --> 07:29.380
It's okay. I'm sorry for 
ambushing you like this.

07:29.820 --> 07:34.010
Anyway, I'll go ahead to school.

07:34.010 --> 07:36.430
You don't want to be seen together, right?

07:36.430 --> 07:39.370
Uh, yeah. Thanks.

07:47.990 --> 07:50.740
What was that all about, anyway?

07:50.740 --> 07:53.180
Wait, was she jealous?

07:53.650 --> 07:55.120
Nah, no way.

07:55.960 --> 07:58.820
But I've never seen her look like that before.

07:59.900 --> 08:02.440
I want to make Shirakawa-san happy.

08:03.160 --> 08:07.170
I'll spend the week 
crafting the perfect date for her!

08:14.040 --> 08:16.390
Hurry up, hurry up!

08:17.570 --> 08:20.110
Harajuku is Runa's jam.

08:20.110 --> 08:25.230
If you don't know where to go, 
just head to Harajuku. She'll lose it.

08:25.770 --> 08:27.110
You weren't kidding!

08:27.110 --> 08:30.400
Harajuku is so awesome!

08:32.860 --> 08:34.570
<b>Bubble Tea Specialty Shop</b>

08:34.570 --> 08:36.530
Here you go.

08:36.910 --> 08:38.220
Thanks.

08:42.500 --> 08:44.210
It's so good!

08:45.910 --> 08:48.540
Runa is super into bubble tea.

08:48.540 --> 08:51.150
I'm telling you, she can drink it nonstop.

08:51.150 --> 08:54.710
We try out all of the popular drinks together.

08:54.710 --> 08:58.220
Every once in a while it feels good 
to get into serious bubble, you know?

08:58.990 --> 09:01.640
Bubble tea is the best!

09:01.640 --> 09:04.170
<i>It's just like Yamana-san said!</i>

09:04.170 --> 09:05.660
How much was it?

09:06.600 --> 09:08.560
I'll pay for my half.

09:08.560 --> 09:11.390
Ah, it's good! It's on me.

09:11.390 --> 09:12.890
What? But...

09:12.890 --> 09:15.320
Today we're celebrating your birthday.

09:17.060 --> 09:20.660
Can't say no to that. Thanks, Ryuto!

09:20.940 --> 09:24.880
Shirakawa-san, what do you think 
of this bubble tea?

09:24.880 --> 09:27.440
What do I think? It's good.

09:27.440 --> 09:28.700
Hmm, hmm.

09:29.880 --> 09:33.210
<i>Harajuku Bubble Tea</i>

09:30.440 --> 09:33.210
Huh? What is that? Oh, crazy!

09:33.210 --> 09:39.640
<i>I can't even count how many 
bubble teas I drank this week.</i>

09:40.180 --> 09:44.490
The milk in this bubble tea is really rich, 
but it still has a prominent tea aroma.

09:44.490 --> 09:46.750
The size and texture of 
the tapioca pearls are just right.

09:46.750 --> 09:48.940
So overall, this one has the best balance.

09:48.940 --> 09:51.060
That's why I wanted you to drink it first.

09:51.060 --> 09:52.670
Using this as a point of reference,

09:52.670 --> 09:55.480
if you want one that's sweeter overall, 
I recommend Tapioca Monster.

09:55.480 --> 09:58.540
For a stronger tea flavor profile 
and lighter milk feel, I'd say Kocharo.

09:56.150 --> 10:03.080
<b>For a stronger tea flavor profile and lighter milk feel, I'd say Kocharo</b>

09:56.150 --> 10:03.080
<b>Or if you like chewier tapioca pearls, we can walk a bit</b>

09:58.540 --> 10:02.170
Or if you like chewier tapioca pearls, 
we can walk a bit to Prupru.

10:02.170 --> 10:05.420
If you want something stronger than milk, 
I would recommend Tiger Cafe's brown sugar tea.

10:05.420 --> 10:06.410
It's really rich!

10:11.840 --> 10:13.690
<i>Crap! I did that thing again!</i>

10:13.690 --> 10:15.740
<i>Oh no! That was beyond gross!</i>

10:15.740 --> 10:18.130
<i>She's slowly backing away 
to the other side of the world!</i>

10:18.610 --> 10:23.560
W-Wow, Ryuto. You like bubble tea that much?

10:23.560 --> 10:27.240
Huh? Uh... yeah. I mean, well,

10:27.600 --> 10:33.680
I heard that you like bubble tea, 
so I studied to get ready for today.

10:33.680 --> 10:36.740
I wanted to take you 
to the kind of shops you'd like.

10:36.740 --> 10:40.200
Huh? You mean you did this just for me?

10:40.200 --> 10:45.910
No, well, I wanted to be able 
to like one thing that I knew you liked.

10:47.600 --> 10:52.250
<i>What now? She's probably grossed out 
by my creepy, nervous, virgin-like babbling!</i>

10:56.460 --> 11:00.640
Really? Nobody's ever said 
something like that to me!

11:00.640 --> 11:02.360
Thank you, Ryuto!

11:05.950 --> 11:10.360
I have a feeling today's bubble tea 
is gonna be the best I've ever had!

11:10.360 --> 11:13.480
Okay, let's go to all of the other shops!

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Sweetness

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Texture

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Size

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Really chewy!!

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Super Sweet

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Super Soft

11:29.410 --> 11:31.870
Tiger Cafe Total

11:31.870 --> 11:34.080
Thank you very much!

11:36.260 --> 11:38.800
Hey, wait. Aren't you having some, Ryuto?

11:38.800 --> 11:41.510
I've already got plenty
 sloshing around in me.

11:41.920 --> 11:43.900
But this one's really good.

11:44.310 --> 11:46.970
Okay, I'll give you one sip of mine.

11:46.970 --> 11:47.990
Huh?

11:48.930 --> 11:52.890
You don't want any? Are you really that full?

11:52.890 --> 11:57.860
N-No! I'll try some. Thanks.

12:11.250 --> 12:15.270
Well? Isn't cheese foam and rock salt godly?

12:19.720 --> 12:21.880
That's an indirect kiss.

12:21.880 --> 12:24.090
<b>Indirect Kiss</b>

12:24.090 --> 12:27.140
You're bright red!

12:29.680 --> 12:35.270
<i>Right now, spending time 
with my girlfriend, I feel so happy!</i>

12:38.110 --> 12:40.280
Now I feel all tea-ed up!

12:40.280 --> 12:42.820
I've never felt this satisfied before.

12:46.780 --> 12:50.410
<i>Oh, right. I have to tell her about Kurose-san.</i>

12:52.050 --> 12:53.250
Uh...

12:53.250 --> 12:54.560
You know, I—

12:53.250 --> 12:54.560
I just—

12:56.400 --> 12:57.710
What is it?

12:57.710 --> 13:00.300
Huh? What did you want?

13:00.300 --> 13:02.060
Huh? Well, I just...

13:02.060 --> 13:04.020
What? What's is it?

13:04.470 --> 13:06.060
Here. A present.

13:06.060 --> 13:08.680
I'm so happy! Thank you!

13:09.490 --> 13:10.400
Oh.

13:10.400 --> 13:11.850
What is it, Ryuto?

13:16.450 --> 13:18.840
Actually, Shirakawa-san,

13:19.350 --> 13:20.150
I'm sorry!

13:22.000 --> 13:25.820
I wanted to let you pick out 
a birthday present,

13:26.580 --> 13:30.700
but I only have 1,000 yen left. 
Is there anything you want for 1,000 yen?

13:34.500 --> 13:38.210
Can I have this? This is what I want!

13:38.210 --> 13:40.420
Harajuku Bubble Tea

13:38.760 --> 13:40.420
This is amazing!

13:40.420 --> 13:42.630
And it's the only one in the world.

13:42.990 --> 13:48.380
Nobody's done anything like this for me 
before. I want to keep it as a memento.

13:48.380 --> 13:53.100
You put in so much effort for me. 
It's like a sign of your love!

13:53.100 --> 13:55.420
Shirakawa-san...

13:56.060 --> 14:00.700
I'll take good care of it, so will you take me 
on another bubble tea date sometime?

14:01.270 --> 14:05.360
Of course! But I'll update it for next time.

14:05.360 --> 14:08.140
There might be some new shops by then.

14:09.840 --> 14:14.660
Thanks, Ryuto! My first day
 being 17 was perfect!

14:33.240 --> 14:35.970
You hear about that 
Shirakawa Runa chick in Class A?

14:36.380 --> 14:38.030
Yeah, I heard.

14:38.030 --> 14:41.440
She gets boyfriends to do her bidding,
and then jumps onto the next guy.

14:41.440 --> 14:43.580
Talk about nasty.

14:44.990 --> 14:49.860
I heard that Shirakawa-san never even 
touches her wallet on dates.

14:49.860 --> 14:53.330
Wicked! No wonder the boys run away.

14:53.910 --> 14:55.800
<i>What's that all about?</i>

14:56.620 --> 15:00.840
<i>Shirakawa-san has always
 attracted a lot of rumors.</i>

15:00.840 --> 15:03.250
<i>This time feels different, though.</i>

15:03.920 --> 15:05.770
<i>Who would spread rumors like those?</i>

15:06.710 --> 15:08.520
What's up, Kasshi?

15:08.520 --> 15:09.770
You aren't eating?

15:10.180 --> 15:12.230
If you don't, then I will.

15:18.200 --> 15:19.000
May I be excused?

15:19.000 --> 15:20.190
See ya, Kasshi!

15:20.190 --> 15:22.020
Huh? Hey!

15:22.760 --> 15:26.010
As soon as I show up, they run away? Why?

15:26.010 --> 15:29.030
Wh-Why? I don't have a clue.

15:29.370 --> 15:31.640
Runa told me about the date.

15:31.640 --> 15:33.990
You're a real freak, huh.

15:33.990 --> 15:36.250
Th-Thank you very much.

15:36.250 --> 15:37.950
That ain't a compliment.

15:38.240 --> 15:41.660
It was all because of your help. 
I wanted to thank you.

15:41.660 --> 15:45.130
I don't care about that, 
but there's something else.

15:45.130 --> 15:46.170
Did you hear them, too?

15:47.030 --> 15:49.380
You mean the rumors about Shirakawa-san?

15:49.690 --> 15:53.590
So you did. Seriously, 
who the hell would do that?

16:01.490 --> 16:03.610
Kashima-kun, good morning.

16:03.610 --> 16:06.380
Huh? Oh. Yeah, good morning.

16:06.900 --> 16:10.110
Oh. Kashima-kun, do you want one?

16:10.110 --> 16:13.700
Huh? Oh. Thanks.

16:16.990 --> 16:20.140
I'm real sorry. I forgot my textbook.

16:20.140 --> 16:21.960
Oh. Yeah, no problem.

16:21.960 --> 16:23.640
We're right here.

16:23.640 --> 16:25.900
No we're not. We're here.

16:27.960 --> 16:32.540
Oh, whoops! I left the print-outs in my office.

16:29.380 --> 16:41.350
Natsume
 Soseki

16:32.540 --> 16:34.460
I'll go get them, so hold on a minute.

16:35.160 --> 16:37.210
Just be quiet, okay?

16:42.400 --> 16:44.350
Hey, Kashima-kun.

16:44.350 --> 16:46.180
Y-Yeah, what is it?

16:46.560 --> 16:48.770
I'm sorry about what happened.

16:48.770 --> 16:49.720
Huh?

16:50.230 --> 16:55.270
Back then, I didn't really 
understand dating and all that.

16:57.660 --> 16:59.400
But now, I think I do understand

16:59.880 --> 17:01.640
how special you are, Kashima-kun.

17:01.640 --> 17:02.620
Huh?

17:02.620 --> 17:04.440
What?!

17:05.210 --> 17:08.320
<i>What does she mean? No, wait. Think carefully.</i>

17:08.320 --> 17:11.990
<i>If I take this the wrong way, 
it'll be like junior high all over again!</i>

17:12.420 --> 17:15.880
<i>But right or wrong, I still can't right now!</i>

17:16.840 --> 17:20.190
Thank you. But I already have a girlfriend.

17:20.190 --> 17:21.060
Huh?

17:23.000 --> 17:26.630
You do? Who is it? Someone here at school?

17:27.020 --> 17:28.240
Um...

17:28.240 --> 17:32.480
Hey, come on. I won't tell anyone. Who is it?

17:37.480 --> 17:38.620
Actually...

17:38.740 --> 17:40.240
Yuna

17:38.740 --> 17:40.240
Nicole went on a date with that dork from class

17:41.330 --> 17:43.220
I can't tell you. Sorry.

17:47.970 --> 17:51.380
<i>If anyone finds out that 
Shirakawa-san and I are dating,</i>

17:51.660 --> 17:56.340
<i>if that was out in the open, 
people would make fun of her.</i>

18:06.670 --> 18:08.160
Yeah? What's up?

18:08.160 --> 18:10.690
So, you wanna go out with me?

18:12.400 --> 18:15.440
I have a boyfriend. Sorry.

18:15.440 --> 18:19.720
Huh? I thought you were single. 
That's what Akari said.

18:19.720 --> 18:23.310
Yeah, I haven't told Akari about it yet.

18:23.310 --> 18:26.620
So who's your boyfriend?
A guy here at school?

18:29.160 --> 18:31.420
It's a secret. But no biggie.

18:31.420 --> 18:33.500
Then why won't you tell me?

18:33.500 --> 18:36.570
You don't want people to know who?

18:36.570 --> 18:38.060
<i>That's exactly it.</i>

18:38.060 --> 18:39.270
Not at all.

18:39.760 --> 18:42.720
I'm totally cool with telling people.

18:43.130 --> 18:46.640
But my boyfriend's super shy.

18:46.640 --> 18:48.410
What the hell does that mean?

18:48.410 --> 18:52.100
What kind of guy wouldn't want 
to brag about dating you?

18:53.030 --> 18:54.520
My secret.

18:54.520 --> 18:58.420
Oh, hold on. You mean 
he's some kind of total loser?

18:58.920 --> 19:03.490
If you're dating someone that boring, it makes 
sense that you're too embarrassed to say.

19:04.120 --> 19:07.620
I don't think my boyfriend is boring at all.

19:08.580 --> 19:15.310
He says he doesn't want to tell people, 
so I just want to respect his feelings.

19:16.180 --> 19:21.290
For me, even if the whole world knew, 
I wouldn't be embarrassed at all!

19:23.140 --> 19:24.740
<i>Shirakawa-san!</i>

19:29.830 --> 19:31.080
<i>For a second there,</i>

19:31.080 --> 19:36.650
<i>I thought Shirakawa-san really didn't 
want people to know that we're dating.</i>

19:36.650 --> 19:38.120
<i>I'm so ashamed of myself.</i>

19:39.160 --> 19:40.300
Kasshi!

19:40.650 --> 19:44.120
Hurry up and finish your class duties, bro!

19:44.120 --> 19:47.070
Give me a minute. I'll be done soon.

19:47.070 --> 19:48.580
Here, Kashima-kun.

19:48.920 --> 19:52.190
I'll turn it in after I fill out my parts. 
You can go ahead home.

19:52.190 --> 19:55.760
But hey, did you hear 
the rumors about Shirakawa-san?

19:55.760 --> 19:56.540
Huh?

19:56.920 --> 20:01.930
Actually, one of my friends is 
Shirakawa-san's ex-boyfriend.

20:01.930 --> 20:07.220
He said that when they were dating, 
he got really worn out.

20:07.550 --> 20:13.440
She led boys on all the time and 
always expects the boy to pay for dates.

20:13.840 --> 20:16.150
She's just a really selfish person.

20:17.200 --> 20:21.500
Are you sure he was talking 
about Shirakawa-san?

20:21.500 --> 20:23.610
Yeah, that's what he said.

20:26.040 --> 20:27.830
I'll pay for my half.

20:28.370 --> 20:30.700
This is what I want!

20:33.170 --> 20:34.380
Kurose-san,

20:35.160 --> 20:37.760
did you tell anyone else about this?

20:37.760 --> 20:42.170
Huh? Um... I kinda forgot.

20:42.680 --> 20:46.140
But don't you think everybody should know?

20:48.600 --> 20:51.470
Shirakawa-san is really popular, right?

20:51.470 --> 20:58.390
Whenever her boyfriend runs out of money, 
she trades him in for the next guy in line.

20:58.390 --> 21:00.860
And like, I heard other stuff too.

21:00.860 --> 21:02.060
Thanks!

21:03.400 --> 21:06.860
Quit saying bad things about Shirakawa-san!

21:07.360 --> 21:10.240
Oh gosh. What's wrong, Kashima-kun?

21:10.240 --> 21:12.710
That ex is lying.

21:13.080 --> 21:15.480
Shirakawa-san isn't like that at all!

21:16.040 --> 21:21.550
Shirakawa-san truly cares about her 
boyfriend and is always thinking about him.

21:21.550 --> 21:23.460
She's the perfect girlfriend!

21:24.520 --> 21:26.590
What boyfriend is that?

21:27.410 --> 21:29.080
Who are you talking about?

21:29.930 --> 21:32.390
Hey, do you know him, Kashima-kun?

21:32.720 --> 21:33.750
Do you?

21:41.360 --> 21:43.350
Shirakawa-san's boyfriend...

21:43.900 --> 21:45.370
is me!

23:26.400 --> 23:28.010
On the next <i>Our Dating Story</i>,

23:28.010 --> 23:31.930
the other, inexperienced you 
gets jealous of the experienced you.

23:32.760 --> 23:36.470
Jealousy. Yes, 'tis the spice of love.

23:36.920 --> 23:38.060
Or whatevs.

23:38.060 --> 23:40.060
<b>Our Jealousy Story: The Inexperienced You Gets Jealous of the Experienced You</b>
